      aesthetic_sensitivity: [66, 0.5, "s", "A"],
      // [src_fitzgerald_usc_life, src_fitzgerald_wilson1922, src_fitzgerald_princeton_gatsby, src_fitzgerald_uscpress_trimalchio, src_fitzgerald_yale_dimock, src_fitzgerald_usc_screenplays | 1917-1938 | university-library biography + contemporary critic + university-library curators + university press + university lecturer + library page on the MGM archive] The USC biography says Scribner's first rejection of his first novel asked that it be resubmitted when revised, and that it was revised and rejected again before the 1919 rewrite; the 1922 essay reports that when others laughed at a catastrophic passage in the first version of The Beautiful and Damned he laughed at it himself and improvised a burlesque; Princeton and the University of South Carolina Press show Gatsby extensively rewritten in galley proof after the typescript went to Perkins. Against that, Wai Chee Dimock reads his reply to Perkins's criticism of Gatsby's vagueness (Perkins's letter is dated 20 November 1924 and the reply 20 December 1924) as deliberate and stubborn, and the MGM page shows him resisting a collaborator's role. Responsive to criticism in revision, firm where he judged the conception central; the evidence cuts both ways, one anecdote comes from a critic's account and the letters are known only through a lecture, so mid-range with a dual-edged impact at modest confidence. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): not lowered; scored conservatively at the outset because the evidence points both ways and no single episode carries the row.
      belief_updating: [58, 0.46, "i", "D"],
      // [src_fitzgerald_usc_screenplays, src_fitzgerald_yale_dimock | 1924-1938 | library page on the MGM archive + university lecturer] The MGM archive page records that on 4 September 1937 Fitzgerald asked the producer Joseph Mankiewicz to let him work alone on the Three Comrades revisions and Mankiewicz agreed, calling the submitted pages 'simply swell'; that after the studio assigned E. E. Paramore as collaborator, who saw himself as an equal partner, Fitzgerald wrote on 24 October that he preferred to keep responsibility for the script as a whole; that he resented Mankiewicz's later interference; and that in early 1938 he was assigned to write Infidelity alone; Wai Chee Dimock reads his December 1924 reply to his editor as holding to his own conception of Gatsby. Two documented episodes in film and a scholar's reading of one in fiction, but both film episodes come from one library page that gives Fitzgerald's side far more fully than the studio's, and the assignment of a collaborator was the studio's decision, so inference-level at modest confidence with a dual-edged impact. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 64/0.50 to 60/0.46 and relabelled inference (single-source dependence; Fitzgerald's own words relayed through one page).
      autonomy_need: [60, 0.46, "i", "D"],
