      source: "Musee Carnavalet - Histoire de Paris (Paris Musees Collections), record S1873, 'Portrait de Sir John Franklin (1786-1847), marin et explorateur anglais': bronze medallion by Pierre-Jean David d'Angers (1788-1856), signed 'DAVID / 1829' and inscribed 'Captain / Franklin R.N.', cast by Louis Richard, 12.5 cm in diameter, purchased by the museum in 1882; the museum's own record states 'CC0 Paris Musees / Musee Carnavalet - Histoire de Paris' and offers the image for download, with no conflicting restriction, and the Wikimedia Commons file of the museum's photograph (photographer Eric Emo, original 2942 x 3000 pixels) is tagged CC0. The record does not say whether Franklin sat for the medallion. The photograph was cropped only to remove the white margin and downscaled once to 1200 x 1183 (never upscaled).",
